\f1\b \cf0 \
Action Import, Action Index & Action Link\
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f0\b0 \cf0 \
Three folder action scripts to import, index or link to new files and folders. Use the script "Enable Folder Actions.scpt" to enable folder actions and afterwards the script "Attach Script to Folder.scpt" to attach the action scripts to one or more folders (those scripts are located in the folder "/Library/Scripts)". \
\
The Finder's contextual menu of Mac OS X 10.3 (or later) also provides the commands "Enable Folder Actions", "Attach a Folder Action..." and "Configure Folder Actions..." and therefore you don't need the mentioned scripts.\
\
\ul Note:\ulnone  It's recommended to copy all folder action scripts to the directory "/Library/Scripts/Folder Action Scripts".\
\
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f1\b \cf0 Add page from Safari/DEVONagent\
Add image from Safari/DEVONagent\
Add linked images from Safari/DEVONagent (to downloads)\
Add links from Safari/DEVONagent (to downloads)\
Add selection from Safari/DEVONagent\
Add text from Safari/DEVONagent\
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f0\b0 \cf0 \
Eight scripts to add the currently displayed page or image, the selection or the text of the current page, the linked images of the current thumbnail gallery or the links of the current page from Safari or DEVONagent to DEVONthink Pro or its download manager. To use them, activate the script menu extra (see "/Utilities/AppleScript/Install Script Menu" or "/Utilities/AppleScript/AppleScript Utility") and copy the scripts afterwards to the folder "~/Library/Scripts/" or copy the scripts to the folder "~/Library/Application Support/DEVONagent/Scripts".\
\
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\li820\ri814\slleading40\ql\qnatural
\cf0 \ul \ulc2 TIP (Mac OS X 10.3.x only):\ulnone \
If you create a sub-folder named \'d2Applications\'d3 inside \'d2~/Library/Scripts/\'d3, you can put application-specific scripts within sub-folders of this folder. These scripts will afterwards appear at the top level of the Scripts menu when the application is frontmost.\
\
For example, if you put the "Add... from Safari" scripts in \'d2~/Library/Scripts/Applications/Safari/\'d3, those scripts will appear at the top level of the menu when Safari is frontmost.\cf2 \
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural
